  "id": "COMPOUND:17901 - PROTEIN:6154",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential mechanism by which 6'-O-Z-Para-Methoxycinnamoylharpagide may interact with Prelamin-A/C. This compound is known to target CMP-N-acetylneuraminate-beta-1,4-galactoside alpha-2,3-sialyltransferase, an enzyme involved in the synthesis of sialic acid. This enzyme is a target of multiple compounds, including (1R,8S,9R,16R)-8,16-bis(4-hydroxyphenyl)-9-[(1R,8S,9R,16R)-4,6,12-trihydroxy-8,16-bis(4-hydroxyphenyl)-15-oxatetracyclo[8.6.1.02,7.014,17]heptadeca-2(7),3,5,10(17),11,13-hexaen-9-yl]-15-oxatetracyclo[8.6.1.02,7.014,17]heptadeca-2(7),3,5,10(17),11,13-hexaene-4,6,12-triol and (3aR,6S,6aR)-3,6-bis(3,4,5-trimethoxyphenyl)-1,3,3a,4,6,6a-hexahydrofuro[3,4-c]furan. These compounds are known to inhibit the sialyltransferase enzyme, which is critical for the proper assembly of sialic acid on glycoproteins, including Prelamin-A/C. The evidence suggests that 6'-O-Z-Para-Methoxycinnamoylharpagide may act through a similar mechanism, targeting this enzyme and potentially affecting the structure or function of Prelamin-A/C. The final score indicates a moderate level of confidence in this relationship, but further experimental validation is needed to confirm the direct interaction and the specific role of the enzyme in the biological process.",
